# Era 1, The Exchange: the witness (e1.w), Ilo at the Sheaf, year 12, day 40 of the hard winter, rent night,
# telling Tomas how he got his name. Story lead, W2-F, 2026-10-22. DRAFT, every line awaiting the author.
# Design: design/eras/era1.md section 4. Ilo saw the loft, the census table, the supper through the window, the
# hands going up the hill road and Osby fair. He heard the board's rule from Abel, Kel's story from Old Tesk and
# Ketti's death from Dorrah. He never knew what was said in the board room or what Bet told Edie Brack.
# He does not tell Tomas whose Anni is: the omission is declared unwitnessed below.
# After the last beat the dispatch goes to e1.end, era 1's end and the single link into era 2's start (q.start).

@witness e1.w.ilo
who: ILO
listener: TOMAS
guest: q_class inspector=ABEL militia=JOSH
place: q_sheaf
opens: e1.w.ilo.open
dispatch: e1.w.ilo.next
reach: q1_loft, q1_census, q1_supper_yard, q_post, q_hill, q1_osby, q1_barns, q_haldane, q_sheaf
sources: ABEL, TESK, DORRAH
never: q1_board, q1_backstore
beat: e1.w.ilo.name | e1.named, e1.per_af, e1.per_letter | seen q1_census ? has(e1.named)
beat: e1.w.ilo.rule | e1.rule_passed, said.e1_abel_tenant, e1.tenant_asked | heard ABEL ? has(e1.rule_passed)
beat: e1.w.ilo.supper | e1.toast_heard, said.e1_raise, said.e1_leave_glass, e1.glass_raised, e1.glass_left | seen q1_supper_yard ? has(e1.toast_heard)
beat: e1.w.ilo.kel | e1.kel_kept, e1.kel_walked, said.e1_abel_sweepings, said.e1_josh_tip | heard TESK ? has(e1.kel_kept) | has(e1.kel_walked)
beat: e1.w.ilo.frost | e1.sallis_sent, e1.sallis_kept, said.e1_abel_loft, said.e1_josh_carter | seen q_post ? has(e1.sallis_sent) | has(e1.sallis_kept)
beat: e1.w.ilo.ketti | e1.sallis_sent | heard DORRAH ? has(e1.sallis_sent)
beat: e1.w.ilo.bowls | e1.door_down, e1.loft_taken | seen q1_osby ? has(e1.door_down)
last: e1.w.ilo.coin
unwitnessed: said.e1_josh_words | the board room: Ilo was never in it, and Abel never told him what Brack said there
unwitnessed: e1.per_af | whose Anni is: Ilo knew, and never told Tomas; he skips it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the opening: the slip
@node e1.w.start
cost: 0
do: var.era = 2; witness(e1.w.ilo)
go: e1.w.ilo.open

@node e1.w.ilo.open
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
camera: near
nar: Years on. The Sheaf, Mill Street, on a winter evening, the back room. It's rent night, and the window behind Ilo is black with the cold.
nar: Ilo Haldane is at the back table with a half he's made last since six. Tomas has been sent to fetch him home and has sat down on the bench instead, in a brown coat too big for him with the cuffs turned back twice.
nar: Mr Furrowe is at the end of the back table, old now, with the rent book open and the coins in stacks. A Hesh tenant doesn't knock at the Furrowe front door. The rent comes to the Sheaf. {when: q_class == inspector}
nar: On his stool at the end of the bar, where he always is, old Josh Brack, retired off the post, with a pint and his back to the room. {when: q_class == militia}
line: TOMAS: Why's it Haldane, though. Why's it not something proper.
line: ILO: What's proper.
line: TOMAS: Something that's a name. Pruett. Sallis.
nar: Ilo goes in his coat and gets out a bit of paper folded so small and so often it's gone soft, like cloth, and puts it on the table, and opens it out flat with the side of his hand.
line: ILO: That's your name. That's where it come from. Read it me.
line: TOMAS: Haldane, I. After the farm.
line: ILO: After the farm.
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.next
cost: 0
alt: e1.end ? seen(e1.w.ilo.coin)
do: wnext()
alt: e1.w.ilo.name ? wat(e1.w.ilo.name)
alt: e1.w.ilo.rule ? wat(e1.w.ilo.rule)
alt: e1.w.ilo.supper ? wat(e1.w.ilo.supper)
alt: e1.w.ilo.kel ? wat(e1.w.ilo.kel)
alt: e1.w.ilo.frost ? wat(e1.w.ilo.frost)
alt: e1.w.ilo.ketti ? wat(e1.w.ilo.ketti)
alt: e1.w.ilo.bowls ? wat(e1.w.ilo.bowls)
go: e1.w.ilo.coin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the beats
@node e1.w.ilo.name
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: TOMAS: I know it's because of the farm. Why'd you let him?
line: ILO: There was a queue right out the door, and it was raining.
line: TOMAS: That's not why.
line: ILO: Mr Furrowe was stood in the door with his hat in his hands. Like it was church. {when: has(e1.per_af) & !has(e1.per_letter)}
line: ABEL: Somebody had to tell the man how to spell it. {when: q_class == inspector & has(e1.per_af) & !has(e1.per_letter)}
line: ILO: Mr Furrowe sent a letter. He didn't come. Mott had it under his hand the whole time like a card he was keeping. {when: has(e1.per_letter)}
line: ABEL: I had the horse to see to. {when: q_class == inspector & has(e1.per_letter)}
nar: Ilo looks at the old man for a second, and doesn't say anything to that. {when: q_class == inspector}
line: ILO: I said put Haldane. I said it. He had the pen over the paper. I thought, if it's going on there anyway, I'll be the one that said it.
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.rule
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: ILO: They'd a meeting up at the registrar's. Mr Furrowe told me after, in the loft. Hands aren't resident. First frost, if you've no roof, you go back up.
line: TOMAS: Up the hill?
line: ILO: Up the hill. In October.
line: ILO: And a tenant's resident. That was in it as well. So I was a tenant by the Sunday. {when: has(e1.tenant_asked)}
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.supper
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: ILO: There was a supper. Orme's big barn. We ate in the yard, we always ate in the yard. You could see in through the window. A ham the size of you.
line: TOMAS: Did you get any?
line: ILO: I got the fat off it. There was a man from Arlen made a speech, and they all laughed.
line: TOMAS: What did he say?
line: ILO: He said we'd sing at a funeral.
nar: The men at the next table have heard it. One of them laughs, and stops.
line: TOMAS: We would, though.
line: ILO: We would. That's why it was funny.
line: ILO: Every glass in that barn went up. I watched them all go up. {when: has(e1.glass_raised)}
line: ILO: Every glass in that barn went up but one. I don't know why I remember that. Nobody else noticed. {when: has(e1.glass_left)}
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.kel
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: ILO: Old Tesk told me this one. His Kel swept the mill. Took a bit of barley off the floor in his boots for his dad's chest.
line: ILO: Orme had him strapped in the back store. Six. Kel came back and sat in the barns and couldn't lie down on it for a week, and he laughed when anybody asked him. {when: has(e1.kel_kept)}
line: ILO: Orme had him walked to the post in his bare feet with his boots in his hands. They put the barley in a bag and wrote on it. Barred off the plain. He's never been down since. {when: has(e1.kel_walked)}
line: TOMAS: For sweepings.
line: ILO: That's what Tesk said. For sweepings.
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.frost
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: ILO: The first frost, they read the list at the post. Every name. I went down to see them off, the Sallises and the Pruetts.
line: ILO: Mr Brack read it. He read it like he was reading the price of oats. {when: q_class == inspector}
line: ILO: The sergeant's dad read it. {when: q_class == militia}
nar: At the bar, old Josh doesn't turn round. {when: q_class == militia}
line: ILO: Arn Sallis got kept. Mr Furrowe said he'd room over the horse. Arn stood on the verge with Ketti and the lad and watched the rest go up. He's never said a word about it to me, not once since. {when: has(e1.sallis_kept) & has(said.e1_abel_loft)}
line: ILO: Arn Sallis got kept. Orme took him on carting, at two-thirds. Gedge's dad never carted for Orme again. {when: has(e1.sallis_kept) & has(said.e1_josh_carter)}
line: ILO: Arn and Ketti went up with the rest. And the lad, Davin. Ketti stopped halfway up to cough and Arn waited for her. {when: has(e1.sallis_sent)}
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.ketti
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
nar: Ilo turns his glass round on the table, a quarter turn at a time.
line: ILO: Dorrah told me at the cup, in the spring. Ketti died up there in the winter. In January. In the hut at the top, with the snow on the door.
line: TOMAS: Of the cough?
line: ILO: Of the cold. Of the cough. Of up there. Arn came down the next harvest with just the lad.
nar: At the bar, old Josh Brack picks up his pint and drinks some of it, and puts it down again in the same ring. {when: q_class == militia}
nar: At the end of the table, Mr Furrowe goes on counting the coins into stacks. He loses his count and starts the stack again. {when: q_class == inspector}
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.w.ilo.bowls
place: q_sheaf
speaker: ILO
cost: 0
line: ILO: And then I married your mum. And we went to Osby fair with the money and she bought the bowls. And me and your grandad Carrow took the door off the end barn for the table, and we dropped it twice.
line: TOMAS: Why five bowls, when there was only three of you?
line: ILO: Your gran said buy five.
line: TOMAS: Why?
line: ILO: Because then there was you, and then there was Aaron. Two on the shelf, turned over, waiting. And then you came, and then he came, and that was all of them.
go: e1.w.ilo.next

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the last beat, and the link into era 2
@node e1.w.ilo.coin
place: q_sheaf
speaker: TOMAS
cost: 0
do: wend()
line: TOMAS: Mum says come now. You're to mind the yard.
line: ILO: I'm to mind the yard.
nar: Mr Furrowe finishes the count and writes it in the book. Then he takes one coin off the last stack and pushes it back across the table toward Ilo with one finger, without a word. Ilo leaves it where it is. Tomas looks at the coin, and then at his dad, and then at the coin. {when: q_class == inspector}
nar: Old Josh Brack puts a coin on the bar for Ilo's half without turning round, and the landlord slides it along. Ilo leaves it where it is. Tomas looks at the coin, and then at his dad, and then at the coin. {when: q_class == militia}
go: e1.w.ilo.next

@node e1.end
cost: 0
do: var.era = 2
go: q.start

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- era 2's class, carried over from era 1
# q.start.class jumps here when era 1 set q_class: Abel's line becomes Ned's day, Josh's becomes Will's.
@node e1.carry.ned
place: q_tower
cost: 0
do: become(q.ned)
nar: Winter. Edrin, the Upper Town.
nar: Ned Furrowe's day. Abel's son. District inspector now. He signs the returns.
go: q.wide

@node e1.carry.will
place: q_tower
cost: 0
do: become(q.will)
nar: Winter. Edrin, the Upper Town.
nar: Will Brack's day. Josh's son. Sergeant of militia now. He keeps the cells and the road post.
go: q.wide
